      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not provide a general definitional statement that “ethnic bias” is specifically “a tendency to favor or judge people differently because of their ethnic group.” It instead reports observed bias patterns measured in medical students toward New Zealand European vs Māori peoples.",
        "The packet supports that implicit and explicit bias and beliefs about warmth/competence/compliance were measured, but it does not explicitly support the claim that such bias “contribut[es] to unequal decisions and outcomes” (beyond a broad statement that racial/ethnic bias has the potential to influence health outcomes and inequities)."
